About WPP Media

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships - all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open - we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. 

WPP Media is WPP's AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.

For more information, visit wppmedia.com .

Overview of Job &nbsp;

Media Planning Executives are responsible for analyzing data, thinking creatively, and developing innovative strategies to ensure marketing campaigns reach the right target audience in the most effective way possible. Armed with this critical analysis, media planning managers devise, propose, or recommend strategies for using certain media effectively to attract and retain customers, increase brand recognition, and maintain customer satisfaction and loyalty. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Responsibilities of the Role &nbsp;

• Audience research in syndicated and first-party data sources. &nbsp;

• Creative spec management. &nbsp;

• Support in creating tactical presentations and actual media plans. &nbsp;

• Oversee the successful launch of campaigns using the “Launch Tracker.” &nbsp;

• QA of media plan setup conducted by various Activation team members. &nbsp;

• Collate/draft commentary on media performance and conduct first review on quality. &nbsp;

• Adhere to team quality standards for reporting templates and delivery. &nbsp;

• Keep consistent track of campaign performance and targets (monthly) across all channels, flagging needs for intervention. &nbsp;

• Use understanding of campaign and marketplace to contribute ideas for campaign experiments and prioritize experiments contributed by other team members. &nbsp;

• Use understanding of campaign performance to contribute content to campaign wrap-up presentations. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

What We’re Looking for &nbsp;

• At least 1 year of experience in digital media or advertising. &nbsp;

• Working knowledge and effective vocabulary across search, social, display, video, and/or programmatic media buying. &nbsp;

• Experience with Media Research Tools (Comscore, GWI, TGI, YouGov, Keyword Planner). &nbsp;

• Expertise with Google Suite - Slides, Sheets, Docs, and LookerStudio. &nbsp;

• Strong organizational skills with a keen ability to prioritize and multitask. &nbsp;

• Proven problem-solving skills and ability to think outside the box. &nbsp;

• Ability to work independently and collaborate in a team environment. &nbsp;

• Detail-oriented and responsive, deadline-driven with strong reasoning skills. &nbsp;

• Proficient in handling and analyzing large datasets, with the ability to create effective visualizations tailored to answer specific analytical questions. &nbsp;

• Be a team player. &nbsp;

• Strong communication skills, capable of collaborating effectively within a large, dynamic team. &nbsp;

• Be enthusiastic and proactive in getting involved. &nbsp;

• A curious mind. &nbsp;

• Strong attention to detail. &nbsp;

• Ability to work to deadlines. &nbsp;

• Able to multitask and handle multiple projects at one time. &nbsp;

• Good organizational skills. &nbsp;

• Good knowledge of PowerPoint and Excel. &nbsp;

• Show interest and understanding of the media industry. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

